workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Let $P=(a,\ln(2a))$, where $a>0$. The derivative is $\frac1x$, so the tangent gradient is $\frac1a$. Its gradient from the origin to $P$ is $\frac{\ln(2a)}a$.
$\begin{align*}\frac1a&=\frac{\ln(2a)}a\\\ln(2a)&=1\\2a&=e\\a&=\frac e2\end{align*}$
Thus $P=\left(\frac e2,1\right)$, and the tangent is
$\begin{align*}y-1&=\frac2e\left(x-\frac e2\right)\\y&=\frac2e x.\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{standardRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,->] (-0.35,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-1.5)--(0,2.1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[black,thick,<->,domain=0.12:3.1,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{ln(2*\x)});
\path (3.55,1.35) node[anchor=north west,inner sep=0pt] {$y=\ln(2x)$};
\draw[standardRed,thick] (0,0)--(2.5,{5/exp(1)});
\path (3.55,2.35) node[anchor=south west,inner sep=0pt] {$y=\frac2e x$};
\fill[black] ({exp(1)/2},1) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({exp(1)/2},1) node[above left] {$P\left(\frac e2,1\right)$};
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Let the point of contact be $(b,e^{4b})$. The derivative gives $m=4e^{4b}$. Since the tangent passes through the origin, its gradient is also $\frac{e^{4b}}b$, with $b\neq0$.
$\begin{align*}4e^{4b}&=\frac{e^{4b}}b\\4b&=1\\b&=\frac14\\m&=4e\end{align*}$
The point of contact is $\left(\frac14,e\right)$.

$\begin{align*}\frac{dy}{dx}&=4\sin x\cos x\\m&=4\sin\frac\pi4\cos\frac\pi4=2\end{align*}$
The tangent is $y-1=2\left(x-\frac\pi4\right)$. At $A$, $y=0$.
$\begin{align*}-1&=2\left(x-\frac\pi4\right)\\x&=\frac\pi4-\frac12=\frac{\pi-2}{4}\end{align*}$
The normal has gradient $-\frac12$, so its equation is $y-1=-\frac12\left(x-\frac\pi4\right)$. At $B$, $x=0$.
$y=1+\frac\pi8=\frac{\pi+8}{8}$
Thus $OA=\frac{\pi-2}{4}$ and $OB=\frac{\pi+8}{8}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=20mm,y=20mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{standardBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{standardRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{standardGreen}{HTML}{4F9B63}
\draw[black,->] (-0.18,0)--(1.65,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,->] (0,-0.2)--(0,2.35) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[standardBlue,thick,domain=-0.1:1.5,samples=90,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2*(sin(\x r))^2});
\path (1.4,2.04) node[above] {$y=2\sin^2x$};
\draw[standardRed,thick] (0,-0.570796)--(1.35,2.129204);
\draw[standardGreen,thick] (-0.1,1.442699)--(1.55,0.617699);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,{1+pi/8})--({pi/4-0.5},0);
\fill[black] ({pi/4},1) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({pi/4},1) node[right] {$P$};
\fill[black] ({pi/4-0.5},0) circle (1.5pt);
\path ({pi/4-0.5},0) node[below right] {$A$};
\fill[black] (0,{1+pi/8}) circle (1.5pt);
\path (0,{1+pi/8}) node[left] {$B$};
\path (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The axes are perpendicular, so
$\begin{align*}\text{Area}&=\frac12\times OA\times OB\\&=\frac12\times\frac{\pi-2}{4}\times\frac{\pi+8}{8}\\&=\frac{(\pi-2)(\pi+8)}{64}\text{ square units}.\end{align*}$

development.question_text:
The diagram shows the curve $y = e^{x}$ and the tangent to the curve at the point $P$ where the curve crosses the $y$-axis.
The tangent meets the $x$-axis at $A$, and $O$ is the origin.
Find the equation of the tangent and the area of $\triangle OAP$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.9,0) -- (2.1,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.3) -- (0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.5:1.6, smooth, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{exp(\x)});
\node[left] at (1.42,4.5) {$y=e^{x}$};
\draw (-1.9,-0.9) -- (1.7,2.7);
\node[below right] at (1.2,2.2) {tangent};
\fill (0,1) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (0,1) {$P$};
\fill (-1,0) circle (2pt);
\node[below left] at (-1,0) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (0,0) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The diagram shows the curve $y = e^{2x}$ and the normal to the curve at the point $P$ where the curve crosses the $y$-axis.
The normal meets the $x$-axis at $B$.
Find the equation of the normal at $P$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.2,0) -- (3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.0) -- (0,5.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.6:0.78, smooth, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{exp(2*\x)});
\node[right] at (0.85,4.4) {$y=e^{2x}$};
\draw (-0.8,1.4) -- (2.6,-0.3);
\node[below] at (2.35,-0.18) {normal};
\fill (0,1) circle (2pt);
\node[above left] at (0,1) {$P$};
\fill (2,0) circle (2pt);
\node[above right] at (2,0) {$B$};
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

